Z||000013||Philphine||11-11-2001||05:02 PM||||i have an 8" in the passenger foot well like stimpy's but smaller. i admit though i'm not happy with it anymore (my truck had a big system and i didn't like the step down). already working on a different system.<P>i also have the center console box for another fiero but i haven't put it in yet. when i put it in my paperwork will go in a soft type briefcase that i can put behind either seat. i've always had one in my other fiero. it's good for that purpose.||||reg||1
Z||000014||stimpy||11-11-2001||07:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LoW_KeY:<BR><B>That's it!! ooh I like it! care to share your box dimensions?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>that looks like it'd work rather good! is that an 8 or a 10? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>As far as dimensions go, that's pretty hard to give because it is a curved fiberglass enclosure that conforms to the footwell's contour. See here for details... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005771.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005771.html</A> <BR>It is a 10" Polk Audio sub, and yeah, it works great. Would work even better if I ponied up for a real amp.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||helmet1978||11-11-2001||07:29 PM||||Well, havent had too many complaints, but there is more room than it looks like. If you have long legs like me you can put your feet in front of the box, and if you have short legs you can put your feet on the front corners of the box. I really should have put a grille on there though because the foam gasket thing (not the speaker surround) got kinda messed up but its mostly cosmetic anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Paul Heindselman<BR>Southwest Idaho Fiero Club<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2M6 - Red<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2M6 - Black (For Sale)<BR>2000 Grand Am GT Sedan - White||||reg||1
